# Fast retriggers of long rings: gong and bell hits at P2 255 every 32nd note on the two voices of the kick track, so
# every hit from the third on steals a ringing voice, which must fade out in a few milliseconds and let the new hit
# start at once (the device behaviour kit v1 got wrong). Then a 32nd-note roll of one glass key.
tempo 140
steps 20
tail 1.5
track kick
preset 223 255 0 0 255 0 0 0 128 0 128 200 0 128 100 255 0 0
note 0 41 0.5 127
note 0.5 44 0.5 120
note 1 41 0.5 127
note 1.5 48 0.5 110
note 2 41 0.5 127
note 2.5 53 0.5 100
param p1 191 3
note 3 60 0.5 127
note 3.5 60 0.5 127
note 4 60 0.5 127
note 4.5 64 0.5 127
param p1 255 6
param p2 120 6
note 8 72 0.5 127
note 8.5 72 0.5 110
note 9 72 0.5 100
note 9.5 72 0.5 90
note 10 72 0.5 80
note 10.5 72 0.5 70
note 11 72 0.5 60
note 11.5 72 0.5 50
# end: two dead wood hits per track, together, steal the ringing voices (they fade in 2.9 ms, the wood ends at once)
track kick
param p1 0 12
param p2 0 12
note 16 53 1 90
note 16 53 1 90
expect sound 0 12
expect peak_below 0
expect idle 26
